    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d512">

                <pb facs="0562" n="458" xml:id="pg458"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.00 Revolutions/145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Culbertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-07-08T12:00:00-05:00">July 8,
                            1932—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:11 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>126. Dávila is Provisional President this morning but with uncertain and probably
                    short tenure. Ibañez is holding aloof. His support is increasing and his policy
                    seems to be to wait until public opinion demands his return to power. Belief is
                    general that this will be soon.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
